00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:22.902
What is it?

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.904
Have you been able
to really unpack

00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:26.839
maybe now that you've
stepped away from it?

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:29.542 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like what is it that
causes that group

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:31.077
think amongst these people,

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:34.046
who so often seemingly vote
against their own interests?

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:36.315 align:start size:88% position:13%
They cannot be happy
that the homeless people

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.484
are now climbing up
the Hollywood Hills

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:40.486
like we're in "Walking Dead."

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:44.657
- No, it is absolutely true,
but there's certain things,

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:46.592 align:start size:84% position:16%
there certainly breaks
walls between them.

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.327
For instance, in San Francisco,

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:50.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
the rich people are
living in Silicon Valley.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.665 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, the rich people
are not living in the places

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:54.467
that they let go down the drain.

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:58.070
There is, you know, it's a
funny thing because in a way,

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.406
in a way, it's a
point that Marx,

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:02.208
Karl Marx himself might've made.

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:04.510
You know, Karl Marx
basically believed

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.914 align:start size:97% position:3%
that your wages had not got,
you hadn't become richer

00:09:07.914 --> 00:09:10.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
if there was now a
bigger divide between you

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:12.184
and the really rich people.

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:13.753
He believed that it was
all relative, you know?

00:09:13.753 --> 00:09:15.555
So even though you
were doing better,

00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:17.757 align:start size:84% position:16%
if the next guy was
doing 10 times better,

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:19.025
you were gonna be unhappy.

00:09:19.025 --> 00:09:20.259
And there's a lot of
human truth to that.

00:09:20.259 --> 00:09:23.462 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, that's, it's
envy, it's covetousness.

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.364
Those are just human traits.

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:27.733
And so we have got a moment now

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:31.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
when some of these wealthy
people are so wealthy,

00:09:31.103 --> 00:09:32.605
and so detached,

00:09:32.605 --> 00:09:35.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so surrounded by other
people like themselves,

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:40.413
and so disdainful of the
ordinary men and women

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:43.115
who just wanna do their
jobs and have some fun

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:45.251
and get married and have kids.

00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:46.953 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're so distasteful
of that life

00:09:46.953 --> 00:09:49.689
that they really have no idea
what people are talking about.

00:09:49.689 --> 00:09:51.757 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Some of these people
who are accusing,

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:54.994 line:0%
look, I've lived out of the
country for seven years.

00:09:54.994 --> 00:09:57.630 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
This is the least
racist country on Earth.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.799 align:start size:84% position:16%
It is the least racist
country on Earth.

00:09:59.799 --> 00:10:01.801 align:start size:84% position:16%
And when they talk
about systemic racism,

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:04.537
it's the least systemic
racist country on Earth.

00:10:04.537 --> 00:10:07.306 align:start size:97% position:3%
'Cause obviously, there are
always gonna be racist people,

00:10:07.306 --> 00:10:09.241
but they don't know it.

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.076
They don't know it.

00:10:10.076 --> 00:10:11.277
When they talk about,

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:12.478 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Oh yeah, these people
are just racist."

00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:14.080
They believe it because
they never see them.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.748 align:start size:88% position:13%
They never meet them,
they never talk to them,

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.016
they never listen to them.

00:10:17.016 --> 00:10:19.518
Some of the stuff that
you and I talk about

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:23.289
on what is now called
conservative media,

00:10:23.289 --> 00:10:24.357
they've never heard.

00:10:24.357 --> 00:10:25.858
They have never heard it.

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:28.861
And when they discover it,
they're absolutely shocked.

00:10:28.861 --> 00:10:30.196 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, Russell
Brand, the comedian,

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:32.598 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, yeah.
- He was a very bright guy,

00:10:32.598 --> 00:10:34.934
but he is kind of
left to center.

00:10:34.934 --> 00:10:37.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
When he found out that the
Russian collusion thing

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.472
was a hoax, he went on
the air and he said,

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:41.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm gobsmacked, I'm
flabbergasted. Who knew?"

00:10:41.941 --> 00:10:43.209
Well, we knew.

00:10:43.209 --> 00:10:44.210 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, we knew and
we said it all the time,

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.212
and a lot of stuff that we know

00:10:46.212 --> 00:10:49.515
ultimately becomes mainstream,
but they never stop and say,

00:10:49.515 --> 00:10:52.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh gee, the right-wingers
were telling the truth,

00:10:52.351 --> 00:10:55.254
and the New York Times and
CNN and NBC were all lying."

00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:56.489
They just never say that.

00:10:57.957 --> 00:10:59.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
Think of all the people
that they made into idols,

00:10:59.792 --> 00:11:01.961
Andrew Cuomo, you know,

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:04.964 align:start size:88% position:13%
what was the other
guy's, Michael Avenatti.

00:11:04.964 --> 00:11:06.265 align:start size:72% position:28%
- You know.
- Yup.

00:11:06.265 --> 00:11:07.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Was that his name, yeah?
- Yup, yup.

00:11:07.433 --> 00:11:10.403 align:start size:84% position:16%
- And now, Dr. Fauci,
torturing dogs,

00:11:10.403 --> 00:11:12.805 align:start size:88% position:13%
having eating the
faces of dogs. (laughs)

00:11:12.805 --> 00:11:15.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Literally, like you
cannot make this stuff up.

00:11:15.174 --> 00:11:16.976 align:start size:88% position:13%
Eating the faces of dogs
(Andrew laughs)

00:11:16.976 --> 00:11:18.878
that they don't let
their paws go to,

00:11:18.878 --> 00:11:21.147
I mean, it's just insane.

00:11:21.147 --> 00:11:22.682
- And these are their heroes.

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:25.351
And, you know, you'd think
at some point they would say,

00:11:25.351 --> 00:11:27.853
"Hmm, maybe we're not that
good a judge of character.

00:11:27.853 --> 00:11:29.522
You know, maybe we ought
to take another look at it.

00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:31.390
At Ted Cruz, maybe
he's not a bad guy.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:33.192 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, maybe
picking on Mike Pence

00:11:33.192 --> 00:11:34.493
for being true to his wife

00:11:34.493 --> 00:11:37.363 align:start size:84% position:16%
isn't really a
great look for us."

00:11:37.363 --> 00:11:39.098
They never do, they
never listen to us,

00:11:39.098 --> 00:11:40.733
they're so separated.

00:11:40.733 --> 00:11:43.135 align:start size:84% position:16%
They're so sequestered
by their wealth

00:11:43.135 --> 00:11:45.471
and their cultural power
more than anything else.

00:11:45.471 --> 00:11:48.074
Their cultural power
has sequestered them

00:11:48.074 --> 00:11:50.676
that they do not know
what they do not know

00:11:50.676 --> 00:11:53.412
and that's basically the kind
of stuff that the rest of us

00:11:53.412 --> 00:11:54.647
are talking about.

00:11:54.647 --> 00:11:56.182 align:start size:84% position:16%
You and I don't
agree on everything.

00:11:56.182 --> 00:11:57.483
Me and Ben Shapiro don't
agree and Michael Knowles.

00:11:57.483 --> 00:11:58.851
We all have these big arguments.

00:11:58.851 --> 00:12:01.587 align:start size:84% position:16%
We have a range of
opinions on the right.

00:12:01.587 --> 00:12:03.122
They've just got
this one opinion,

00:12:03.122 --> 00:12:04.590 align:start size:84% position:16%
but they hear it again
and again and again

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:06.092 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they think
everything else is evil.

00:12:06.092 --> 00:12:07.626
- So what's the trick?

00:12:07.626 --> 00:12:09.495
I mean, you know, when I do my
weekly Q and A's on Thursday,

00:12:09.495 --> 00:12:12.231 align:start size:97% position:3%
there's always like 10
questions of the same variety

00:12:12.231 --> 00:12:15.101 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is what are the
tricks to wake up my friend?

00:12:15.101 --> 00:12:16.602
How can I bring them back?

00:12:16.602 --> 00:12:19.505 align:start size:97% position:3%
I can't get them to sit down
and watch a PragerU video

00:12:19.505 --> 00:12:22.475
or Dave, now you're
too scary for them.

00:12:22.475 --> 00:12:24.410
So I assume you're on the
scary list too, Andrew.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.345
Like what are the tricks?

00:12:26.345 --> 00:12:27.580
You got any tricks?

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.482
I mean, you were around
a lot of these people.

00:12:29.482 --> 00:12:32.518 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, two things,
very important.

00:12:32.518 --> 00:12:35.421
One is you've gotta speak up.

00:12:35.421 --> 00:12:36.922
This thing about
dropping our voice.

00:12:36.922 --> 00:12:40.025
You know, I used to go into
movie studios for meetings

00:12:40.025 --> 00:12:41.727
and I'd be sitting out
in the waiting room,

00:12:41.727 --> 00:12:43.863
you sit for a few minutes
before they call you in,

00:12:43.863 --> 00:12:45.798
and almost every time,

00:12:45.798 --> 00:12:47.967
somebody would come up to me
and drop his voice and say,

00:12:47.967 --> 00:12:49.535
"Oi, I saw you on 'Hannity.'

00:12:49.535 --> 00:12:50.936
I saw you on 'Beck.'"

00:12:50.936 --> 00:12:52.138
And I would always
say the same thing.

00:12:52.138 --> 00:12:53.239 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Why are you whispering?
(Dave laughs)

00:12:53.239 --> 00:12:55.407
We're in the right." (laughs)

00:12:55.407 --> 00:12:56.675
And like-
- Right.

00:12:56.675 --> 00:12:58.577
- And I understand the
fear, and I understand,

00:12:58.577 --> 00:13:00.780
you know, we famously had this

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.481
supposedly secret organization,

00:13:02.481 --> 00:13:05.251
The Friends of Abe
out in Hollywood.

00:13:05.251 --> 00:13:06.519
And I kept saying
to the leaders,

00:13:06.519 --> 00:13:08.587
"You know, we've
gotta go public."

00:13:08.587 --> 00:13:10.122
And they wouldn't do it

00:13:10.122 --> 00:13:11.624
'cause they didn't want the
working guys to get caught.

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.926
The gaffers and the guys
who were not movie stars

00:13:13.926 --> 00:13:15.194
and all this.

00:13:15.194 --> 00:13:16.862 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I just thought,
if you don't,

00:13:16.862 --> 00:13:19.698
if you act in secret, then
you look like you're ashamed.

00:13:19.698 --> 00:13:21.767 align:start size:97% position:3%
And if you act in secret,
you look like you're afraid.

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:23.903
And so all of us,
because all of us,

00:13:23.903 --> 00:13:25.838
you know, it's not just artists
who are part of the culture,

00:13:25.838 --> 00:13:27.606
it's not just media people.

00:13:27.606 --> 00:13:29.475
Everybody is part
of the culture.

00:13:29.475 --> 00:13:30.810 align:start size:81% position:19%
Everybody has a
little piece of it

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:32.912
like a candle in their hand.

00:13:32.912 --> 00:13:34.180
You have got to speak up,

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:35.114
You've got to.

00:13:35.114 --> 00:13:36.382
You gotta say it politely,

00:13:36.382 --> 00:13:37.616
you don't have to
scream at people,

00:13:37.616 --> 00:13:38.851
you don't have to
get in their faces,

00:13:38.851 --> 00:13:40.085
you don't have to
be Donald Trump.

00:13:40.085 --> 00:13:43.022
You just politely say,
"You know, I disagree."

00:13:43.022 --> 00:13:45.124
And if we don't
start doing that,

00:13:45.124 --> 00:13:47.927
if we let them cowl
us and silence us,

00:13:47.927 --> 00:13:49.595
we have no choice, chance.

00:13:49.595 --> 00:13:53.532
And the other side of
it also is (chuckles)

00:13:53.532 --> 00:13:56.368 align:start size:97% position:3%
right when you just think that
the truth is so important,

00:13:56.368 --> 00:13:58.270
the facts are so important

00:13:58.270 --> 00:13:59.772 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you don't have
to be nice about them,

00:13:59.772 --> 00:14:02.341
that you can scream an ugly
truth in someone's face.

00:14:02.341 --> 00:14:03.542
And Paul Simon said,

00:14:03.542 --> 00:14:05.544 align:start size:84% position:16%
"You know, I don't
want you to lie to me,

00:14:05.544 --> 00:14:07.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I want some tenderness
beneath your honesty."

00:14:07.479 --> 00:14:09.682
And right-wingers got
to learn that trick

00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:12.852
because the left are ugly.

00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:14.620
They're mean, they
call people names,

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:18.791 align:start position:0%
they're disgusting, they
cancel people, they bully them.

00:14:18.791 --> 00:14:22.595
If we don't have a sort
of civilized attitude,

00:14:22.595 --> 00:14:23.762
when I say civilized,

00:14:23.762 --> 00:14:25.264 align:start size:88% position:13%
that doesn't mean
keeping your mouth shut.

00:14:25.264 --> 00:14:30.102 align:start size:97% position:3%
It means speaking bravely
and clearly in a polite way,

00:14:30.102 --> 00:14:31.937
then we're just
the same as them.

00:14:31.937 --> 00:14:33.405
We get lost in the crowd.

00:14:33.405 --> 00:14:36.642
So if we don't develop
some communication skills

00:14:36.642 --> 00:14:39.912
and some courage, we'll be lost.

00:14:39.912 --> 00:14:41.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be swept away
'cause they own the media.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:42.915
- You know, it's so funny

00:14:42.915 --> 00:14:44.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I obviously
agree with the sentiment,

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:46.151
and then there's this
part of me as someone

00:14:46.151 --> 00:14:49.655 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's sort of new to this
thing on the right, let's say,

00:14:49.655 --> 00:14:53.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
that when you see them
lie and lie and lie again,

00:14:53.192 --> 00:14:55.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
and know they're lying,
and we know they're lying,

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.629
and everyone knows
salt units in quote,

00:14:56.629 --> 00:14:58.230
and they just keep going,

00:14:58.230 --> 00:15:02.368 align:start size:88% position:13%
I can somehow see how
decent right wing people

00:15:02.368 --> 00:15:04.036
that are moderates, really,

00:15:04.036 --> 00:15:07.473
start sounding like
crazy, angry kooks

00:15:07.473 --> 00:15:10.509
because the years go by,
you try to rationalize,

00:15:10.509 --> 00:15:12.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
you try to be open, you
try to have conversations,

00:15:12.711 --> 00:15:15.180 align:start size:88% position:13%
they keep lying, things
keep getting worse,

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.649
they're dragging you
to hell with them,

00:15:16.649 --> 00:15:19.084 align:start size:97% position:3%
next thing you know, you're
screaming on the radio

00:15:19.084 --> 00:15:22.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
for four hours a day about
whatever it might be.

00:15:22.688 --> 00:15:25.190
So I'm sympathetic to, even
though I get your point,

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.759
I am sympathetic to the people

00:15:26.759 --> 00:15:29.862
that it sort of sound like
they're nuts at some level.

00:15:29.862 --> 00:15:32.398
- Me too, and they
also gaslight you.

00:15:32.398 --> 00:15:35.601 align:start size:84% position:16%
So for 30 years,
they call you racist,

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:37.603 align:start size:84% position:16%
they call you sexist,
your god stinks,

00:15:37.603 --> 00:15:39.505
your country stinks,
your history stinks,

00:15:39.505 --> 00:15:40.773
everything about you stinks.

00:15:40.773 --> 00:15:42.741
Then Rush Limbaugh comes
on the air and he says,

00:15:42.741 --> 00:15:44.610 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Well, these feminazis,"
and everybody goes,

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:47.246 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Where is the civility?
- Yeah.

00:15:47.246 --> 00:15:49.448
What has happened to the
civility in this country?"

00:15:49.448 --> 00:15:51.750
So they gaslight you,
but if you listen,

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:53.185
one of the things
that happened to me

00:15:53.185 --> 00:15:55.354 align:start size:97% position:3%
when I came back from
England, where I was living,

00:15:55.354 --> 00:15:56.789
I started listening to Rush

00:15:56.789 --> 00:15:59.291
just to hear what
the fuss was about,

00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:01.126
and he was so happy and so funny

00:16:01.126 --> 00:16:03.729
and so, kind of sweet-natured.

00:16:03.729 --> 00:16:06.065
With all the stuff that
he said that I thought,

00:16:06.065 --> 00:16:07.299
"No, wait a minute.

00:16:07.299 --> 00:16:08.968
All the stuff I heard is untrue

00:16:08.968 --> 00:16:11.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I wanna listen to
what this guy has to say."

00:16:11.603 --> 00:16:12.805
They called him uncivil

00:16:12.805 --> 00:16:15.607 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he could sometimes
go off, obviously,

00:16:15.607 --> 00:16:17.843
but he was actually
a happy warrior.

00:16:17.843 --> 00:16:20.913
And he was a wonderfully
funny and warm person.

00:16:20.913 --> 00:16:22.848
When you, the one time I
talked to him in person,

00:16:22.848 --> 00:16:25.217 align:start size:97% position:3%
he was kind of shy and
sweet-natured and all that.

00:16:25.217 --> 00:16:26.685
It was kind of a shock.

00:16:26.685 --> 00:16:28.988
But still, he had
a knack for that.

00:16:28.988 --> 00:16:30.255
So you're absolutely right.

00:16:30.255 --> 00:16:32.257
I have total sympathy
for why people do it.

00:16:32.257 --> 00:16:33.959 align:start size:88% position:13%
I know why they
supported Donald Trump.

00:16:33.959 --> 00:16:36.795
I told people who were
appalled by Donald Trump,

00:16:36.795 --> 00:16:38.998
"You know, think of them
as the voice of people

00:16:38.998 --> 00:16:42.368 align:start size:88% position:13%
who have been just
insulted for 50 years."

00:16:42.368 --> 00:16:43.869 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Mm-hmm.
- You know, that's what he is.

00:16:43.869 --> 00:16:47.706 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's why they came up with
him and he had his flaws.

00:16:47.706 --> 00:16:49.441
I think they really
hurt him in the end,

00:16:49.441 --> 00:16:51.176
but they also helped
them get where he was,

00:16:51.176 --> 00:16:53.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they made people love
him 'cause he spoke for them.

00:16:53.379 --> 00:16:54.913
But I think we need,

00:16:54.913 --> 00:16:56.548
you know, the thing I liked
about this guy in Virginia,

00:16:56.548 --> 00:16:59.585
